gtz(){return"Investors qualify if they meet certain criteria based on local regulations \u2014 which may include minimum portfolio size and prior investment experience. Our investments are typically available for accredited investors, qualified purchasers, professional clients, or equivalent designations depending on jurisdiction. Please contact us for specific eligibility requirements in your region."},
gta(){return"How does a typical Coinetra investment work?"},
gtb(){return"Coinetra investment vehicles pool capital to invest in specific private equity funds or direct opportunities. Capital calls, distributions, and reporting are managed through our secure platform. We partner with industry-leading administrators and custodians."},
gtc(){return"What's the minimum commitment?"},
gtd(){return"Minimum investment amounts vary by opportunity but generally start at [Your Minimum Amount, e.g., $50,000 or \u20ac50,000]. We aim to provide access with lower minimums than traditional private equity entry points."},
gt2(){return"When is capital drawn on my commitment?"},
gt3(){return"Capital call schedules are determined by the underlying investment managers. Typically, a portion is called upfront, with the remainder drawn over the investment period (often 3-6 years)."},
gts(){return"What's the selection process for opportunities?"},
gtt(){return"We screen investments using rigorous due diligence, focusing on manager track records, strategy, team, and terms. While we target high-quality opportunities, past performance does not guarantee future results."},
